#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:258
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Commit bits allocated prior to the development of the notion of areas of "
"authority may be appropriate for use in many parts of the tree.  However, "
"common sense dictates that a committer who has not previously worked in an "
"area of the tree seek review prior to committing, seek approval from the "
"appropriate responsible party, and/or work with a mentor.  Since the rules "
"regarding code maintenance differ by area of the tree, this is as much for "
"the benefit of the committer working in an area of less familiarity as it is "
"for others working on the tree."
msgstr "在权限区域概念出现之前分配的提交权限，可能适用于代码树的许多部分。不过，常识要求提交者在此前未参与某个代码树区域的工作时，先征求审核、取得相应负责方的批准，和／或与导师合作。由于代码树不同区域的代码维护规则各不相同，这样做既有利于在不熟悉区域工作的提交者，也有利于其他参与代码树工作的人员。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:260
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Committers are encouraged to seek review for their work as part of the "
"normal development process, regardless of the area of the tree where the "
"work is occurring."
msgstr "无论工作属于代码树的哪个区域，都鼓励提交者在正常开发流程中为自己的工作寻求审核。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:261
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Policy for Committer Activity in Other Trees"
msgstr "提交者在其他代码树中的工作政策"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:266
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Committers are trusted to use good judgment when working outside their "
"primary area.  The link:https://www.freebsd.org/internal/cross-repo-commits/"
"[Cross Repo Commit Policy] describes the overall framework.  The following "
"guidelines apply:"
msgstr "项目信任提交者在主要负责区域之外工作时能够运用良好的判断力。link:https://www.freebsd.org/internal/cross-repo-commits/[Cross Repo Commit Policy] 介绍了总体框架。适用以下准则："

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:267
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "General Guidelines"
msgstr "一般准则"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:270
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"These changes do not require review or approval from a committer in the "
"target repository:"
msgstr "以下变更无需目标代码仓库的提交者审核或批准："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:272
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"All committers may modify [.filename]#src/share/misc/committers-*.dot#, [."
"filename]#src/usr.bin/calendar/calendars/calendar.freebsd#, and [."
"filename]#ports/astro/xearth/files#."
msgstr "所有提交者都可以修改 [.filename]#src/share/misc/committers-*.dot#、[.filename]#src/usr.bin/calendar/calendars/calendar.freebsd# 和 [.filename]#ports/astro/xearth/files#。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:273
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"All committers may commit documentation changes to [.filename]#src# files, "
"such as manual pages, READMEs, fortune databases, calendar files, and "
"comment fixes, subject to the normal care and tending of commits."
msgstr "所有提交者都可以对 [.filename]#src# 文件进行文档类修改，例如手册页、README、fortune 数据库、日历文件和注释修正，但提交时仍应遵循通常的谨慎原则。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:274
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Obvious trivial fixes — typos, broken links, and similar trivial corrections "
"— may be committed by any committer to any repository (see also <<doc-"
"blanket-approval>>)."
msgstr "明显且琐碎的修正——拼写错误、失效链接以及类似的小问题——任何提交者都可以提交到任何代码仓库（另请参阅 <<doc-blanket-approval>>）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:275
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When you have recently introduced a build breakage that's trivial to "
"resolve, though a revert and a full review usually is better for anything "
"non-trivial."
msgstr "如果您最近引入了容易修复的构建问题，可以直接修复；但对于非琐碎的问题，通常最好回退变更并进行完整审核。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:276
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Non-Obvious Changes"
msgstr "不明显的变更"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:281
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For changes beyond those described here, committers should seek review from "
"committers with the appropriate bit in the target repository.  When in "
"doubt, seek review, even if you have a commit bit in the repo.  Always test "
"build and test run or read files affected by the change."
msgstr "对于超出此处所述范围的变更，提交者应向目标代码仓库中拥有相应权限的提交者寻求审核。如有疑问，请寻求审核，即使您拥有该代码仓库的提交权限也不例外。务必测试构建和运行，或阅读变更所影响的文件。"

#. type: Title ====
