#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1422
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Keeping current"
msgstr "保持最新"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1428
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So, time passes.  It's time now to update the tree for the latest changes "
"upstream.  When you checkout `main` make sure that you have no diffs.  It's "
"a lot easier to commit those to a branch (or use `git stash`) before doing "
"the following."
msgstr "时间就这样过去了。现在该根据上游的最新更改更新树了。检出 `main` 时，请确保没有未提交的差异。最好先将这些更改提交到一个分支（或使用 `git stash`），再执行以下操作。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1431
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you are used to `git pull`, we strongly recommend using the `--ff-only` "
"option, and further setting it as the default option.  Alternatively, `git "
"pull --rebase` is useful if you have changes staged in the `main` branch."
msgstr "如果你习惯使用 `git pull`，我们强烈建议使用 `--ff-only` 选项，并进一步将其设为默认选项。如果你已在 `main` 分支暂存了更改，也可以使用 `git pull --rebase`。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1435
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git config --global pull.ff only\n"
msgstr "% git config --global pull.ff only\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1438
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You may need to omit the --global if you want this setting to apply to only "
"this repository."
msgstr "如果只想将此设置应用于当前仓库，可能需要省略 --global。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1444
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% cd freebsd-src\n"
"% git checkout main\n"
"% git pull (--ff-only|--rebase)\n"
msgstr "% cd freebsd-src\n% git checkout main\n% git pull (--ff-only|--rebase)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1448
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There is a common trap, that the combination command `git pull` will try to "
"perform a merge, which would sometimes creates a merge commit that didn't "
"exist before.  This can be harder to recover from."
msgstr "有一个常见陷阱：组合命令 `git pull` 会尝试执行合并，有时会创建一个此前不存在的合并提交。这种情况可能更难恢复。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1450
#, fuzzy
msgid "The longer form is also recommended."
msgstr "同样建议使用较长的命令形式。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1457
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% cd freebsd-src\n"
"% git checkout main\n"
"% git fetch freebsd\n"
"% git merge --ff-only freebsd/main\n"
msgstr "% cd freebsd-src\n% git checkout main\n% git fetch freebsd\n% git merge --ff-only freebsd/main\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1462
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"These commands reset your tree to the `main` branch, and then update it from "
"where you pulled the tree from originally.  It's important to switch to "
"`main` before doing this so it moves forward.  Now, it's time to move the "
"changes forward:"
msgstr "这些命令会将你的树重置到 `main` 分支，然后从最初拉取该树的远程更新它。执行这些操作前，切换到 `main` 很重要，这样它才能向前推进。现在该将更改向前迁移了："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1466
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git rebase -i main working\n"
msgstr "% git rebase -i main working\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1473
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This will bring up an interactive screen to change the defaults.  For now, "
"just exit the editor.  Everything should just apply.  If not, then you'll "
"need to resolve the diffs.  https://docs.github.com/en/free-pro-team@latest/"
"github/using-git/resolving-merge-conflicts-after-a-git-rebase[This github "
"document] can help you navigate this process."
msgstr "这会打开交互界面，让你修改默认设置。目前只需退出编辑器即可。所有更改应该都能直接应用。如果不能，你就需要解决差异。 link:https://docs.github.com/en/free-pro-team@latest/github/using-git/resolving-merge-conflicts-after-a-git-rebase[这篇 GitHub 文档]可以帮助你完成此过程。"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1475
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Time to push changes upstream"
msgstr "现在可以将更改推送到上游了"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1478
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First, ensure that the push URL is properly configured for the upstream "
"repository."
msgstr "首先，确保已为上游仓库正确配置推送 URL。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1482
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git remote set-url --push freebsd ssh://git@gitrepo.freebsd.org/src.git\n"
msgstr "% git remote set-url --push freebsd ssh://git@gitrepo.freebsd.org/src.git\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1486
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Then, verify that user name and email are configured right.  We require that "
"they exactly match the passwd entry in FreeBSD cluster."
msgstr "然后，确认用户名和电子邮件地址配置正确。它们必须与 FreeBSD 集群中的 passwd 条目完全一致。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1488
#, fuzzy
msgid "Use"
msgstr "使用"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1492
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "freefall% gen-gitconfig.sh\n"
msgstr "freefall% gen-gitconfig.sh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1495
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"on freefall.freebsd.org to get a recipe that you can use directly, assuming /"
"usr/local/bin is in the PATH."
msgstr "在 freefall.freebsd.org 上运行此命令，以获取可直接使用的配置方案；这需要 /usr/local/bin 位于 PATH 中。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1500
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The below command merges the `working` branch into the upstream `main` "
"branch.  It's important that you curate your changes to be just like you "
"want them in the FreeBSD source repo before doing this.  This syntax pushes "
"the `working` branch to `main`, moving the `main` branch forward.  You will "
"only be able to do this if this results in a linear change to `main` (e.g. "
"no merges)."
msgstr "下面的命令会将 `working` 分支合并到上游的 `main` 分支。在执行之前，务必整理好更改，使其符合你希望提交到 FreeBSD 源代码仓库的状态。此语法会将 `working` 分支推送到 `main`，使 `main` 分支向前推进。只有当这会让 `main` 保持线性历史记录时（例如，没有合并提交），才能执行此操作。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1504
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git push freebsd working:main\n"
msgstr "% git push freebsd working:main\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1507
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If your push is rejected due to losing a commit race, rebase your branch "
"before trying again:"
msgstr "如果推送因提交竞争而被拒绝，请先变基你的分支，再重试："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1514
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout working\n"
"% git fetch freebsd\n"
"% git rebase freebsd/main\n"
"% git push freebsd working:main\n"
msgstr "% git checkout working\n% git fetch freebsd\n% git rebase freebsd/main\n% git push freebsd working:main\n"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1517
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Time to push changes upstream (alternative)"
msgstr "现在可以将更改推送到上游了（另一种方法）"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1522
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Some people find it easier to merge their changes to their local `main` "
"before pushing to the remote repository.  Also, `git arc stage` moves "
"changes from a branch to the local `main` when you need to do a subset of a "
"branch.  The instructions are similar to the prior section:"
msgstr "有些人觉得在推送到远程仓库前，先将更改合并到本地 `main` 更容易。当你只需要处理分支中的一部分更改时，`git arc stage` 也可以将这些更改从分支移到本地 `main`。操作说明与上一节类似："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1527
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout main\n"
"% git merge --ff-only `working`\n"
"% git push freebsd\n"
msgstr "% git checkout main\n% git merge --ff-only `working`\n% git push freebsd\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1530
#, fuzzy
msgid "If you lose the race, then try again with"
msgstr "如果提交竞争失败，请重试以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1534
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git pull --rebase\n"
"% git push freebsd\n"
msgstr "% git pull --rebase\n% git push freebsd\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1537
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"These commands will fetch the most recent `freebsd/main` and then rebase the "
"local `main` changes on top of that, which is what you want when you lose "
"the commit race.  Note: merging vendor branch commits will not work with "
"this technique."
msgstr "这些命令会获取最新的 `freebsd/main`，然后将本地 `main` 上的更改变基到其之上；提交竞争失败时，这正是你需要的操作。注意：使用此方法无法合并供应商分支的提交。"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1538
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Finding the Subversion Revision"
msgstr "查找 Subversion 修订版本"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1542
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You'll need to make sure that you've fetched the notes (see the crossref:"
"committers-guide[git-mini-daily-use, Daily use]for details).  Once you have "
"these, notes will show up in the git log command like so:"
msgstr "你需要确保已获取备注（详情请参见 crossref:committers-guide[git-mini-daily-use, 日常使用]）。获取后，备注会显示在 `git log` 命令的输出中，如下所示："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1546
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git log\n"
msgstr "% git log\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1549
#, fuzzy
msgid "If you have a specific version in mind, you can use this construct:"
msgstr "如果你想查找某个特定版本，可以使用以下形式："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1553
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git log --grep revision=XXXX\n"
msgstr "% git log --grep revision=XXXX\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1557
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"to find the specific revision.  The hex number after 'commit' is the hash "
"you can use to refer to this commit."
msgstr "以查找特定修订版本。`commit` 后的十六进制数字是可用于引用此提交的哈希值。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1559
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Git FAQ"
msgstr "Git 常见问题"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1562
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This section provides a number of targeted answers to questions that are "
"likely to come up often for users and developers."
msgstr "本节针对用户和开发者经常遇到的问题，提供一些有针对性的解答。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1567
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We use the common convention of having the origin for the FreeBSD repository "
"being 'freebsd' rather than the default 'origin' to allow people to use that "
"for their own development and to minimize \"whoops\" pushes to the wrong "
"repository."
msgstr "我们采用常见约定，将 FreeBSD 仓库的远程名称设为 'freebsd'，而不是默认的 'origin'，以便人们将 'origin' 用于自己的开发工作，并尽量避免误将更改推送到错误的仓库。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1569
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Users"
msgstr "用户"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1571
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "How do I track -current and -stable with only one copy of the repository?"
msgstr "如何只用一份仓库副本跟踪 -current 和 -stable？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1576
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** Although disk space is not a huge issue, it's more efficient to use "
"only one copy of the repository.  With SVN mirroring, I could checkout "
"multiple trees from the same repository.  How do I do this with Git?"
msgstr "**问：**虽然磁盘空间不是大问题，但只使用一份仓库副本效率更高。使用 SVN 镜像时，我可以从同一个仓库检出多个树。使用 Git 要怎么做？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1580
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** You can use Git worktrees.  There's a number of ways to do this, but "
"the simplest way is to use a clone to track -current, and a worktree to "
"track stable releases.  While using a 'bare repository' has been put forward "
"as a way to cope, it's more complicated and will not be documented here."
msgstr "**答：**可以使用 Git worktree。实现方式有很多，最简单的方法是用一个克隆来跟踪 -current，再用一个 worktree 跟踪稳定版本。有人提出使用“裸仓库”来解决这个问题，但这种方式更复杂，因此这里不作介绍。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1583
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First, you need to clone the FreeBSD repository, shown here cloning into "
"`freebsd-current` to reduce confusion.  $URL is whatever mirror works best "
"for you:"
msgstr "首先，克隆 FreeBSD 仓库。以下示例将其克隆到 `freebsd-current` 目录，以减少混淆。$URL 是对你来说最合适的镜像地址："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1587
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git clone -o freebsd --config remote.freebsd.fetch='+refs/notes/*:refs/notes/*' $URL freebsd-current\n"
msgstr "% git clone -o freebsd --config remote.freebsd.fetch='+refs/notes/*:refs/notes/*' $URL freebsd-current\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1590
#, fuzzy
msgid "then once that's cloned, you can simply create a worktree from it:"
msgstr "克隆完成后，就可以直接从中创建一个 worktree："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1595
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% cd freebsd-current\n"
"% git worktree add ../freebsd-stable-12 stable/12\n"
msgstr "% cd freebsd-current\n% git worktree add ../freebsd-stable-12 stable/12\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1599
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"this will checkout `stable/12` into a directory named `freebsd-stable-12` "
"that's a peer to the `freebsd-current` directory.  Once created, it's "
"updated very similarly to how you might expect:"
msgstr "这会将 `stable/12` 检出到名为 `freebsd-stable-12` 的目录中，该目录与 `freebsd-current` 目录同级。创建后，可以按预期的方式更新它："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1609
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% cd freebsd-current\n"
"% git checkout main\n"
"% git pull --ff-only\n"
"# changes from upstream now local and current tree updated\n"
"% cd ../freebsd-stable-12\n"
"% git merge --ff-only freebsd/stable/12\n"
"# now your stable/12 is up to date too\n"
msgstr "% cd freebsd-current\n% git checkout main\n% git pull --ff-only\n# 现在，上游的更改已在本地，当前树也已更新\n% cd ../freebsd-stable-12\n% git merge --ff-only freebsd/stable/12\n# 现在，stable/12 也已更新\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1612
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I recommend using `--ff-only` because it's safer and you avoid accidentally "
"getting into a 'merge nightmare' where you have an extra change in your "
"tree, forcing a complicated merge rather than a simple one."
msgstr "我建议使用 `--ff-only`，因为这样更安全，可以避免意外陷入“合并噩梦”：树中多出一个更改，导致需要进行复杂合并，而不是简单合并。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1614
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Here's https://adventurist.me/posts/00296[a good writeup] that goes into "
"more detail."
msgstr "link:https://adventurist.me/posts/00296[这里有一篇不错的文章]，提供了更多详细信息。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1615
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Developers"
msgstr "开发者"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1617
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Ooops! I committed to `main`, instead of another branch."
msgstr "糟了！我提交到了 `main`，而不是另一个分支。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1620
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** From time to time, I goof up and mistakenly commit to the `main` "
"branch. What do I do?"
msgstr "**问：**我偶尔会犯错，误将提交放到了 `main` 分支。该怎么办？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1622
#, fuzzy
msgid "**A:** First, don't panic."
msgstr "**答：**首先，不要慌。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1626
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Second, don't push.  In fact, you can fix almost anything if you haven't "
"pushed.  All the answers in this section assume no push has happened."
msgstr "其次，不要推送。事实上，只要还没有推送，几乎任何问题都能修复。本节中的所有解答都假设你尚未推送。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1628
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The following answer assumes you committed to `main` and want to create a "
"branch called `issue`:"
msgstr "以下解答假设你提交到了 `main`，并想创建一个名为 `issue` 的分支："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1634
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout -b issue              # Create the 'issue' branch\n"
"% git checkout -B main freebsd/main  # Reset main to upstream\n"
"% git checkout issue                 # Back to where you were\n"
msgstr "% git checkout -b issue              # 创建 'issue' 分支\n% git checkout -B main freebsd/main  # 将 main 重置到上游版本\n% git checkout issue                 # 返回原来的位置\n"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1636
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Ooops! I committed something to the wrong branch!"
msgstr "糟了！我把某项更改提交到了错误的分支！"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1640
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** I was working on feature on the `wilma` branch, but accidentally "
"committed a change relevant to the `fred` branch in 'wilma'.  What do I do?"
msgstr "**问：**我在 `wilma` 分支上开发某项功能时，误将与 `fred` 分支相关的更改提交到了 `wilma`。该怎么办？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1644
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** The answer is similar to the previous one, but with cherry picking.  "
"This assumes there's only one commit on wilma, but will generalize to more "
"complicated situations.  It also assumes that it's the last commit on wilma "
"(hence using wilma in the `git cherry-pick` command), but that too can be "
"generalized."
msgstr "**答：**解决方法与上一个问题类似，但要使用 cherry-pick。以下假设 `wilma` 上只有一个提交，但此方法也适用于更复杂的情况。还假设该提交是 `wilma` 上的最后一个提交（因此在 `git cherry-pick` 命令中使用 wilma），不过这一点也可以推广。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1652
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# We're on branch wilma\n"
"% git checkout fred\t\t# move to fred branch\n"
"% git cherry-pick wilma\t\t# copy the misplaced commit\n"
"% git checkout wilma\t\t# go back to wilma branch\n"
"% git reset --hard HEAD^\t# move what wilma refers to back 1 commit\n"
msgstr "# 当前位于 wilma 分支\n% git checkout fred\t\t# 切换到 fred 分支\n% git cherry-pick wilma\t\t# 复制误提交的更改\n% git checkout wilma\t\t# 切回 wilma 分支\n% git reset --hard HEAD^\t# 将 wilma 指向的位置回退 1 个提交\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1655
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If it is not the last commit, you can cherry-pick that one change from wilma "
"onto fred, then use `git rebase -i` to remove the change from wilma."
msgstr "如果该提交不是最后一个提交，可以将那项更改从 wilma cherry-pick 到 fred，然后使用 `git rebase -i` 从 wilma 中移除该更改。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1662
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# We're on branch wilma\n"
"% git checkout fred\t\t\t# move to fred branch\n"
"% git cherry-pick HASH_OF_CHANGE\t# copy the misplaced commit\n"
"% git rebase -i main wilma\t\t# drop the cherry-picked change\n"
msgstr "# 当前位于 wilma 分支\n% git checkout fred\t\t\t# 切换到 fred 分支\n% git cherry-pick HASH_OF_CHANGE\t# 复制误提交的更改\n% git rebase -i main wilma\t\t# 删除 cherry-pick 过来的更改\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1665
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** But what if I want to commit a few changes to `main`, but keep the "
"rest in `wilma` for some reason?"
msgstr "**问：**如果我想将几项更改提交到 `main`，但出于某些原因想把其余更改保留在 `wilma`，该怎么办？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1671
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** The same technique above also works if you are wanting to 'land' "
"parts of the branch you are working on into `main` before the rest of the "
"branch is ready (say you noticed an unrelated typo, or fixed an incidental "
"bug).  You can cherry pick those changes into `main`, then push to the "
"parent repository.  Once you've done that, cleanup couldn't be simpler: just "
"`git rebase -i`.  Git will notice you've done this and skip the common "
"changes automatically (even if you had to change the commit message or tweak "
"the commit slightly).  There's no need to switch back to wilma to adjust it: "
"just rebase!"
msgstr "**答：**如果你想在分支中的其余更改尚未准备好之前，先将部分更改“合入” `main`，上面的方法同样适用（例如，你发现了一处无关的拼写错误，或修复了一个附带的错误）。你可以将这些更改 cherry-pick 到 `main`，然后推送到上游仓库。完成后，清理工作再简单不过了：只需执行 `git rebase -i`。Git 会发现你已经做过这些操作，并自动跳过共有的更改（即使你必须更改提交消息或稍微调整提交内容也一样）。无需切回 wilma 进行调整：直接变基即可！"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1673
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** I want to split off some changes from branch `wilma` into branch "
"`fred`"
msgstr "**问：**我想把分支 `wilma` 中的一部分更改拆分到分支 `fred`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1679
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** The more general answer would be the same as the previous.  You'd "
"checkout/create the `fred` branch, cherry pick the changes you want from "
"`wilma` one at a time, then rebase `wilma` to remove those changes you "
"cherry picked.  `git rebase -i main wilma` will toss you into an editor, and "
"remove the `pick` lines that correspond to the commits you copied to "
"`fred`.  If all goes well, and there are no conflicts, you're done.  If not, "
"you'll need to resolve the conflicts as you go."
msgstr "**答：**更通用的做法与上一个问题相同。检出或创建 `fred` 分支，将你想从 `wilma` 移过去的更改逐个 cherry-pick 过来，然后对 `wilma` 变基，以移除已 cherry-pick 的更改。`git rebase -i main wilma` 会打开编辑器；删除与复制到 `fred` 的提交对应的 `pick` 行。如果一切顺利且没有冲突，就完成了。否则，你需要在过程中解决冲突。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1684
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The other way to do this would be to checkout `wilma` and then create the "
"branch `fred` to point to the same point in the tree.  You can then `git "
"rebase -i` both these branches, selecting the changes you want in `fred` or "
"`wilma` by retaining the pick likes, and deleting the rest from the editor.  "
"Some people would create a tag/branch called `pre-split` before starting in "
"case something goes wrong in the split.  You can undo it with the following "
"sequence:"
msgstr "另一种做法是检出 `wilma`，然后创建分支 `fred`，使其指向树中的同一位置。接着可以对这两个分支执行 `git rebase -i`，通过保留 `pick` 行并在编辑器中删除其余行，来选择要保留在 `fred` 或 `wilma` 中的更改。有些人会在开始前创建一个名为 `pre-split` 的标签或分支，以防拆分过程中出错。你可以按以下顺序撤销操作："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1691
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout pre-split\t# Go back\n"
"% git branch -D fred\t\t# delete the fred branch\n"
"% git checkout -B wilma\t\t# reset the wilma branch\n"
"% git branch -d pre-split\t# Pretend it didn't happen\n"
msgstr "% git checkout pre-split\t# 返回\n% git branch -D fred\t\t# 删除 fred 分支\n% git checkout -B wilma\t\t# 重置 wilma 分支\n% git branch -d pre-split\t# 假装这件事没发生过\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1695
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The last step is optional.  If you are going to try again to split, you'd "
"omit it."
msgstr "最后一步是可选的。如果你打算再次尝试拆分，就不要执行这一步。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1699
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** But I did things as I read along and didn't see your advice at the "
"end to create a branch, and now `fred` and `wilma` are all screwed up.  How "
"do I find what `wilma` was before I started.  I don't know how many times I "
"moved things around."
msgstr "**问：** 可是我一边读一边操作，没看到你在最后建议创建分支，现在 `fred` 和 `wilma` 都弄乱了。我该怎么找回操作前的 `wilma`？我不记得自己移动过多少次了。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1701
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** All is not lost. You can figure out it, so long as it hasn't been too "
"long, or too many commits (hundreds)."
msgstr "**答：** 事情还没到无可挽回的地步。只要时间没有过去太久，提交数量也没有太多（数百个），就能找出它原来的样子。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1705
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So I created a wilma branch and committed a couple of things to it, then "
"decided I wanted to split it into fred and wilma.  Nothing weird happened "
"when I did that, but let's say it did.  The way to look at what you've done "
"is with the `git reflog`:"
msgstr "我创建了一个 wilma 分支，并向其中提交了几项更改，之后决定把它拆成 fred 和 wilma。执行时没有发生什么奇怪的事，但假设确实发生了。你可以通过 `git reflog` 查看自己做过什么："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1720
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git reflog\n"
"6ff9c25 (HEAD -> wilma) HEAD@{0}: rebase -i (finish): returning to refs/heads/wilma\n"
"6ff9c25 (HEAD -> wilma) HEAD@{1}: rebase -i (start): checkout main\n"
"869cbd3 HEAD@{2}: rebase -i (start): checkout wilma\n"
"a6a5094 (fred) HEAD@{3}: rebase -i (finish): returning to refs/heads/fred\n"
"a6a5094 (fred) HEAD@{4}: rebase -i (pick): Encourage contributions\n"
"1ccd109 (freebsd/main, main) HEAD@{5}: rebase -i (start): checkout main\n"
"869cbd3 HEAD@{6}: rebase -i (start): checkout fred\n"
"869cbd3 HEAD@{7}: checkout: moving from wilma to fred\n"
"869cbd3 HEAD@{8}: commit: Encourage contributions\n"
"...\n"
"%\n"
msgstr "% git reflog\n6ff9c25 (HEAD -> wilma) HEAD@{0}: rebase -i (finish): returning to refs/heads/wilma\n6ff9c25 (HEAD -> wilma) HEAD@{1}: rebase -i (start): checkout main\n869cbd3 HEAD@{2}: rebase -i (start): checkout wilma\na6a5094 (fred) HEAD@{3}: rebase -i (finish): returning to refs/heads/fred\na6a5094 (fred) HEAD@{4}: rebase -i (pick): Encourage contributions\n1ccd109 (freebsd/main, main) HEAD@{5}: rebase -i (start): checkout main\n869cbd3 HEAD@{6}: rebase -i (start): checkout fred\n869cbd3 HEAD@{7}: checkout: moving from wilma to fred\n869cbd3 HEAD@{8}: commit: Encourage contributions\n...\n%\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1728
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Here we see the changes I've made.  You can use it to figure out where "
"things went wrong.  I'll just point out a few things here.  The first one is "
"that HEAD@{X} is a 'commitish' thing, so you can use that as an argument to "
"a command.  Although if that command commits anything to the repository, the "
"X numbers change.  You can also use the hash (first column)."
msgstr "这里可以看到我做过的更改。你可以据此找出哪里出了问题。这里我只指出几处。首先，HEAD@{X} 是一种“commitish”对象，可以将它作为命令参数。不过，如果该命令向仓库提交了任何内容，X 的编号就会改变。你也可以使用哈希值（第一列）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1736
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next, 'Encourage contributions' was the last commit I made to `wilma` before "
"I decided to split things up.  You can also see the same hash is there when "
"I created the `fred` branch to do that.  I started by rebasing `fred` and "
"you see the 'start', each step, and the 'finish' for that process.  While we "
"don't need it here, you can figure out exactly what happened.  Fortunately, "
"to fix this, you can follow the prior answer's steps, but with the hash "
"`869cbd3` instead of `pre-split`.  While that seems a bit verbose, it's easy "
"to remember since you're doing one thing at a time.  You can also stack:"
msgstr "接下来，'Encourage contributions' 是我决定拆分内容之前，在 `wilma` 上所做的最后一次提交。创建 `fred` 分支时也能看到相同的哈希值。我先对 `fred` 执行了变基，你可以看到这个过程的“start”、每个步骤以及“finish”。虽然这里用不上这些信息，但你可以据此准确还原发生了什么。所幸，修复方法与前一个回答中的步骤相同，只需使用哈希值 `869cbd3` 替代 `pre-split`。虽然看起来有点啰嗦，但一次只做一件事，很容易记住。你也可以把命令合并起来："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1741
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout -B wilma 869cbd3\n"
"% git branch -D fred\n"
msgstr "% git checkout -B wilma 869cbd3\n% git branch -D fred\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1748
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"and you are ready to try again.  The `checkout -B` with the hash combines "
"checking out and creating a branch for it.  The `-B` instead of `-b` forces "
"the movement of a pre-existing branch.  Either way works, which is what's "
"great (and awful) about Git.  One reason I tend to use `git checkout -B xxxx "
"hash` instead of checking out the hash, and then creating / moving the "
"branch is purely to avoid the slightly distressing message about detached "
"heads:"
msgstr "这样你就可以重新尝试了。`checkout -B` 加上哈希值，会把检出和为其创建分支合并起来。与 `-b` 不同，`-B` 会强制移动已存在的分支。两种方式都行，这正是 Git 既棒又让人头疼的地方。我倾向于使用 `git checkout -B xxxx hash`，而不是先检出哈希值再创建或移动分支，原因很简单：这样可以避免看到关于分离 HEAD 状态的那条令人稍感不安的消息："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1754
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout 869cbd3\n"
"M\tfaq.md\n"
"Note: checking out '869cbd3'.\n"
msgstr "% git checkout 869cbd3\nM\tfaq.md\n注意：正在检出 '869cbd3'。\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1758
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You are in 'detached HEAD' state. You can look around, make experimental\n"
"changes and commit them, and you can discard any commits you make in this\n"
"state without impacting any branches by performing another checkout.\n"
msgstr "你当前处于 'detached HEAD' 状态。可以查看内容、进行实验性更改并提交；之后可以通过再次检出，丢弃在此状态下所做的任何提交，而不会影响任何分支。\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1766
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"HEAD is now at 869cbd3 Encourage contributions\n"
"% git checkout -B wilma\n"
msgstr "HEAD 当前位于 869cbd3 Encourage contributions\n% git checkout -B wilma\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1769
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"this produces the same effect, but I have to read a lot more and severed "
"heads aren't an image I like to contemplate."
msgstr "这样做效果相同，但我得读更多内容，而且我不喜欢想象头颅被斩断的画面。"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1770
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Ooops! I did a `git pull` and it created a merge commit, what do I do?"
msgstr "糟了！我执行了 `git pull`，结果它创建了一个合并提交，该怎么办？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1774
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** I was on autopilot and did a `git pull` for my development tree and "
"that created a merge commit on `main`.  How do I recover?"
msgstr "**问：** 我没多想，就在开发树中执行了 `git pull`，结果在 `main` 上创建了一个合并提交。该怎么恢复？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1776
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** This can happen when you invoke the pull with your development branch "
"checked out."
msgstr "**答：** 如果你在检出开发分支时执行 pull，就可能发生这种情况。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1778
#, fuzzy
msgid "Many developers use `git pull --rebase` to avoid this situation."
msgstr "许多开发者会使用 `git pull --rebase` 来避免这种情况。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1781
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Right after the pull, you will have the new merge commit checked out.  Git "
"supports a `HEAD^#` syntax to examine the parents of a merge commit:"
msgstr "执行 pull 后，你会检出这个新的合并提交。Git 支持使用 `HEAD^#` 语法查看合并提交的父提交："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1786
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"git log --oneline HEAD^1   # Look at the first parent's commits\n"
"git log --oneline HEAD^2   # Look at the second parent's commits\n"
msgstr "git log --oneline HEAD^1   # 查看第一个父提交的提交记录\ngit log --oneline HEAD^2   # 查看第二个父提交的提交记录\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1790
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"From those logs, you can easily identify which commit is your development "
"work.  Then you simply reset your branch to the corresponding `HEAD^#`:"
msgstr "根据这些日志，你可以轻松找出哪些提交是你在开发中的工作。然后，只需将分支重置到相应的 `HEAD^#`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1794
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "git reset --hard HEAD^1\n"
msgstr "git reset --hard HEAD^1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1797
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In addition, a `git pull --rebase` at this stage will rebase your changes to "
"'main' to the latest 'freebsd/main'."
msgstr "此外，在此阶段执行 `git pull --rebase`，会将你对 'main' 所做的更改变基到最新的 'freebsd/main' 上。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1799
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Q:** But I also need to fix my `main` branch. How do I do that?"
msgstr "**问：** 可是我还需要修复 `main` 分支。该怎么做？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1802
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** Git keeps track of the remote repository branches in a `freebsd/` "
"namespace.  To fix your `main` branch, just make it point to the remote's "
"`main`:"
msgstr "**答：** Git 会在 `freebsd/` 命名空间中跟踪远程仓库的分支。要修复 `main` 分支，只需让它指向远程仓库的 `main`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1806
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "git branch -f main freebsd/main\n"
msgstr "git branch -f main freebsd/main\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1811
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There's nothing magical about branches in Git: they are just labels on a "
"graph that are automatically moved forward by making commits.  So the above "
"works because you're just moving a label.  There's no metadata about the "
"branch that needs to be preserved due to this."
msgstr "Git 中的分支并没有什么神奇之处：它们只是图上的标签，会随着提交而自动向前移动。上面的命令之所以有效，是因为你只是在移动一个标签。分支没有需要因此保留的元数据。"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1812
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Mixing and matching branches"
msgstr "混合使用分支"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1816
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** So I have two branches `worker` and `async` that I'd like to combine "
"into one branch called `feature` while maintaining the commits in both."
msgstr "**问：** 我有两个分支 `worker` 和 `async`，想把它们合并到一个名为 `feature` 的分支中，同时保留两个分支上的提交。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1818
#, fuzzy
msgid "**A:** This is a job for cherry pick."
msgstr "**答：** 这时可以使用 cherry-pick。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1824
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout worker\n"
"% git checkout -b feature\t# create a new branch\n"
"% git cherry-pick main..async\t# bring in the changes\n"
msgstr "% git checkout worker\n% git checkout -b feature\t# 创建新分支\n% git cherry-pick main..async\t# 引入更改\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1829
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You now have a new branch called `feature`.  This branch combines commits "
"from both branches.  You can further curate it with `git rebase`."
msgstr "现在你有了一个名为 `feature` 的新分支，其中合并了两个分支的提交。你还可以使用 `git rebase` 进一步整理它。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1831
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** I have a branch called `driver` and I'd like to break it up into "
"`kernel` and `userland` so I can evolve them separately and commit each "
"branch as it becomes ready."
msgstr "**问：** 我有一个名为 `driver` 的分支，想把它拆分为 `kernel` 和 `userland`，以便分别开发，并在每个分支准备就绪时分别提交。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1834
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** This takes a little bit of prep work, but `git rebase` will do the "
"heavy lifting here."
msgstr "**答：** 这需要一些准备工作，不过繁重的部分可以交给 `git rebase` 完成。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1840
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout driver\t\t# Checkout the driver\n"
"% git checkout -b kernel\t# Create kernel branch\n"
"% git checkout -b userland\t# Create userland branch\n"
msgstr "% git checkout driver\t\t# 检出 driver\n% git checkout -b kernel\t# 创建 kernel 分支\n% git checkout -b userland\t# 创建 userland 分支\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1845
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now you have two identical branches.  So, it's time to separate out the "
"commits.  We'll assume first that all the commits in `driver` go into either "
"the `kernel` or the `userland` branch, but not both."
msgstr "现在你有了两个完全相同的分支。接下来要把提交分开。我们先假设 `driver` 上的所有提交都应归入 `kernel` 或 `userland` 分支之一，而不是同时归入两者。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1849
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git rebase -i main kernel\n"
msgstr "% git rebase -i main kernel\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1852
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"and just include the changes you want (with a 'p' or 'pick' line) and just "
"delete the commits you don't (this sounds scary, but if worse comes to "
"worse, you can throw this all away and start over with the `driver` branch "
"since you've not yet moved it)."
msgstr "只保留你需要的更改（使用 'p' 或 'pick' 行），删除不需要的提交（这听起来有点吓人，但即使情况最糟，你也可以放弃这一切，从 `driver` 分支重新开始，因为你还没有移动它）。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1856
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git rebase -i main userland\n"
msgstr "% git rebase -i main userland\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1859
#, fuzzy
msgid "and do the same thing you did with the `kernel` branch."
msgstr "对 `userland` 分支执行与 `kernel` 分支相同的操作。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1862
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** Oh great! I followed the above and forgot a commit in the `kernel` "
"branch.  How do I recover?"
msgstr "**问：** 太好了！我照着上面的步骤做，却忘了在 `kernel` 分支中加入一个提交。该怎么补救？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1865
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** You can use the `driver` branch to find the hash of the commit is "
"missing and cherry pick it."
msgstr "**答：** 你可以通过 `driver` 分支找出遗漏提交的哈希值，然后对它执行 cherry-pick。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1871
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git checkout kernel\n"
"% git log driver\n"
"% git cherry-pick $HASH\n"
msgstr "% git checkout kernel\n% git log driver\n% git cherry-pick $HASH\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1877
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Q:** OK. I have the same situation as the above, but my commits are all "
"mixed up.  I need parts of one commit to go to one branch and the rest to go "
"to the other.  In fact, I have several.  Your rebase method to select sounds "
"tricky."
msgstr "**问：** 好。我遇到的情况和上面相同，但提交都混在一起了。我需要把一个提交中的一部分放到一个分支，剩余部分放到另一个分支。实际上有好几个这样的提交。你用变基来选择提交的方法听起来很棘手。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1880
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** In this situation, you'd be better off to curate the original branch "
"to separate out the commits, and then use the above method to split the "
"branch."
msgstr "**答：** 这种情况下，最好先整理原始分支，将提交分开，然后再用上面的方法拆分分支。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1885
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So let's assume that there's just one commit with a clean tree.  You can "
"either use `git rebase` with an `edit` line, or you can use this with the "
"commit on the tip.  The steps are the same either way.  The first thing we "
"need to do is to back up one commit while leaving the changes uncommitted in "
"the tree:"
msgstr "假设只有一个提交，而且工作树是干净的。你可以使用 `git rebase`，并将其中一行设为 `edit`；也可以直接对分支顶端的提交执行以下操作。无论哪种方式，步骤都相同。首先，我们需要回退一个提交，同时让更改保留在工作树中且不提交："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1889
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git reset HEAD^\n"
msgstr "% git reset HEAD^\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1892
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Note: Do not, repeat do not, add `--hard` here since that also removes the "
"changes from your tree."
msgstr "注意：这里千万不要添加 `--hard`，因为那也会从工作树中删除更改。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1896
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now, if you are lucky, the change needing to be split up falls entirely "
"along file lines.  In that case you can just do the usual `git add` for the "
"files in each group than do a `git commit`.  Note: when you do this, you'll "
"lose the commit message when you do the reset, so if you need it for some "
"reason, you should save a copy (though `git log $HASH` can recover it)."
msgstr "如果运气好，需要拆分的更改恰好完全按文件划分。这时只需照常对各组文件执行 `git add`，然后执行 `git commit`。注意：重置时会丢失提交说明；如果之后还需要它，请先保存副本（不过可以通过 `git log $HASH` 找回）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1899
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you are not lucky, you'll need to split apart files.  There's another "
"tool to do that which you can apply one file at a time."
msgstr "如果运气不好，你就需要拆分文件。还有一个工具可以逐个文件地完成这项工作。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1903
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "git add -i foo/bar.c\n"
msgstr "git add -i foo/bar.c\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1909
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"will step through the diffs, prompting you, one at time, whether to include "
"or exclude the hunk.  Once you're done, `git commit` and you'll have the "
"remainder in your tree.  You can run it multiple times as well, and even "
"over multiple files (though I find it easier to do one file at a time and "
"use the `git rebase -i` to fold the related commits together)."
msgstr "它会逐个显示差异块，并逐次询问你是否要包含该差异块。完成后执行 `git commit`，剩余更改就会留在工作树中。你也可以多次运行它，甚至对多个文件运行（不过我发现每次处理一个文件更容易，再用 `git rebase -i` 将相关提交合并起来）。"

#. type: Title =====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1910
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Joining the FreeBSD GitHub organization."
msgstr "加入 FreeBSD GitHub 组织。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1913
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Q:** How do I join the FreeBSD GitHub organization?"
msgstr "**问：** 如何加入 FreeBSD GitHub 组织？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1917
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** Please see https://wiki.freebsd.org/"
"GitHub#Joining_the_Organisation[our GitHub Wiki Info] page for details.  "
"Briefly, all FreeBSD committers may join.  Those who are not committers who "
"request joining will be considered on a case by case basis."
msgstr "**答：** 详情请参阅 link:https://wiki.freebsd.org/GitHub#Joining_the_Organisation[我们的 GitHub Wiki 信息页面]。简而言之，所有 FreeBSD 提交者都可以加入。非提交者提出加入申请时，将根据具体情况逐案考虑。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1918
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Cloning and Mirroring"
msgstr "克隆与镜像"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1921
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Q:** I'd like to mirror the entire Git repository, how do I do that?"
msgstr "**问：** 我想镜像整个 Git 仓库，该怎么做？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1923
#, fuzzy
msgid "**A:** If all you want to do is mirror, then"
msgstr "**答：** 如果你只想创建镜像，那么"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1927
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git clone --mirror $URL\n"
msgstr "% git clone --mirror $URL\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1931
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"will do the trick.  However, there are two disadvantages to this if you want "
"to use it for anything other than a mirror you'll reclone."
msgstr "就可以了。不过，如果你打算将它用于镜像以外的用途（否则你会重新克隆），这种做法有两个缺点。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1935
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First, this is a 'bare repository' which has the repository database, but no "
"checked out worktree.  This is great for mirroring, but terrible for day to "
"day work.  There's a number of ways around this with `git worktree`:"
msgstr "首先，这是一个“裸仓库”，其中包含仓库数据库，但没有检出的工作树。这很适合镜像，却不适合日常工作。使用 `git worktree` 有多种解决方法："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1943
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git clone --mirror https://git.freebsd.org/ports.git ports.git\n"
"% cd ports.git\n"
"% git worktree add ../ports main\n"
"% git worktree add ../quarterly branches/2020Q4\n"
"% cd ../ports\n"
msgstr "% git clone --mirror https://git.freebsd.org/ports.git ports.git\n% cd ports.git\n% git worktree add ../ports main\n% git worktree add ../quarterly branches/2020Q4\n% cd ../ports\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1946
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"But if you aren't using your mirror for further local clones, then it's a "
"poor match."
msgstr "但如果你不打算用镜像进行后续的本地克隆，那么它就不太合适。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1949
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The second disadvantage is that Git normally rewrites the refs (branch name, "
"tags, etc) from upstream so that your local refs can evolve independently of "
"upstream.  This means that you'll lose changes if you are committing to this "
"repository on anything other than private project branches."
msgstr "第二个缺点是，Git 通常会重写来自上游的 refs（分支名、标签等），使本地 refs 能够独立于上游演进。这意味着，如果你在此仓库中提交的内容不属于私有项目分支，你就会丢失这些更改。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1951
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Q:** So what can I do instead?"
msgstr "**问：** 那我可以怎么做？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1954
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**A:** Well, you can stuff all of the upstream repository's refs into a "
"private namespace in your local repository.  Git clones everything via a "
"'refspec' and the default refspec is:"
msgstr "**答：** 你可以将上游仓库的所有 refs 放到本地仓库的一个私有命名空间中。Git 通过“refspec”克隆所有内容，默认的 refspec 是："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1958
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "        fetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/freebsd/*\n"
msgstr "        fetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/freebsd/*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1961
#, fuzzy
msgid "which says just fetch the branch refs."
msgstr "它表示只获取分支 refs。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1965
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"However, the FreeBSD repository has a number of other things in it.  To see "
"those, you can add explicit refspecs for each ref namespace, or you can "
"fetch everything.  To setup your repository to do that:"
msgstr "不过，FreeBSD 仓库中还有许多其他内容。要获取这些内容，你可以为每个 ref 命名空间添加显式 refspec，也可以获取所有内容。要将仓库配置为获取所有内容："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1969
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "git config --add remote.freebsd.fetch '+refs/*:refs/freebsd/*'\n"
msgstr "git config --add remote.freebsd.fetch '+refs/*:refs/freebsd/*'\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1973
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"which will put everything in the upstream repository into your local "
"repository's `refs/freebsd/` namespace.  Please note, that this also grabs "
"all the unconverted vendor branches and the number of refs associated with "
"them is quite large."
msgstr "这会将上游仓库中的所有内容放入本地仓库的 `refs/freebsd/` 命名空间。请注意，这也会获取所有尚未转换的供应商分支，与之关联的 refs 数量相当多。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1975
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You'll need to refer to these 'refs' with their full name because they "
"aren't in and of Git's regular namespaces."
msgstr "由于这些“refs”不属于 Git 的常规命名空间，因此你需要使用它们的完整名称来引用。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1979
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "git log refs/freebsd/vendor/zlib/1.2.10\n"
msgstr "git log refs/freebsd/vendor/zlib/1.2.10\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1982
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"would look at the log for the vendor branch for zlib starting at 1.2.10."
msgstr "这会查看从 1.2.10 开始的 zlib 供应商分支日志。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1983
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Collaborating with others"
msgstr "与他人协作"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1987
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"One of the keys to good software development on a project as large as "
"FreeBSD is the ability to collaborate with others before you push your "
"changes to the tree.  The FreeBSD project's Git repositories do not, yet, "
"allow user-created branches to be pushed to the repository, and therefore if "
"you wish to share your changes with others you must use another mechanism, "
"such as a hosted GitLab or GitHub, to share changes in a user-generated "
"branch."
msgstr "在 FreeBSD 这样的大型项目中进行良好的软件开发，关键之一是在将更改推送到代码树之前能够与他人协作。目前，FreeBSD 项目的 Git 仓库还不允许将用户创建的分支推送到仓库。因此，如果你想与他人分享更改，就必须使用其他机制，例如托管于 GitLab 或 GitHub 上的仓库，来分享用户创建的分支。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1989
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The following instructions show how to set up a user-generated branch, based "
"on the FreeBSD `main` branch, and push it to GitHub."
msgstr "以下说明将展示如何基于 FreeBSD 的 `main` 分支创建用户分支，并将其推送到 GitHub。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1992
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Before you begin, make sure that your local Git repo is up to date and has "
"the correct origins set crossref:committers-guide[keeping_current,as shown "
"above]."
msgstr "开始之前，请确保本地 Git 仓库已更新，并且已正确设置远程仓库，crossref:committers-guide[keeping_current,如上所示]。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:1998
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git remote -v\n"
"freebsd https://git.freebsd.org/src.git (fetch)\n"
"freebsd ssh://git@gitrepo.freebsd.org/src.git (push)\n"
msgstr "% git remote -v\nfreebsd https://git.freebsd.org/src.git (fetch)\nfreebsd ssh://git@gitrepo.freebsd.org/src.git (push)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2002
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first step is to create a fork of https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-"
"src[FreeBSD] on GitHub following these https://docs.github.com/en/github/"
"getting-started-with-github/fork-a-repo[guidelines].  The destination of the "
"fork should be your own, personal, GitHub account (gvnn3 in my case)."
msgstr "第一步是按照这些 link:https://docs.github.com/en/github/getting-started-with-github/fork-a-repo[指南]，在 GitHub 上为 link:https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-src[FreeBSD] 创建一个分支。分支应位于你自己的 GitHub 个人账户下（以我为例，是 gvnn3）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2004
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now add a remote on your local system that points to your fork:"
msgstr "现在，在本地系统上添加一个指向你分支的远程仓库："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2012
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git remote add github git@github.com:gvnn3/freebsd-src.git\n"
"% git remote -v\n"
"github\tgit@github.com:gvnn3/freebsd-src.git (fetch)\n"
"github\tgit@github.com:gvnn3/freebsd-src.git (push)\n"
"freebsd\thttps://git.freebsd.org/src.git (fetch)\n"
"freebsd\tssh://git@gitrepo.freebsd.org/src.git (push)\n"
msgstr "% git remote add github git@github.com:gvnn3/freebsd-src.git\n% git remote -v\ngithub\tgit@github.com:gvnn3/freebsd-src.git (fetch)\ngithub\tgit@github.com:gvnn3/freebsd-src.git (push)\nfreebsd\thttps://git.freebsd.org/src.git (fetch)\nfreebsd\tssh://git@gitrepo.freebsd.org/src.git (push)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2015
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With this in place you can create a branch crossref:committers-"
"guide[keeping_a_local_branch,as shown above]."
msgstr "完成这些设置后，你就可以创建一个分支，参见 crossref:committers-guide[keeping_a_local_branch,上文所示]。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2019
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% git checkout -b gnn-pr2001-fix\n"
msgstr "% git checkout -b gnn-pr2001-fix\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2023
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Make whatever modifications you wish in your branch.  Build, test, and once "
"you're ready to collaborate with others it's time to push your changes into "
"your hosted branch.  Before you can push you'll have to set the appropriate "
"upstream, as Git will tell you the first time you try to push to your +github"
"+ remote:"
msgstr "在你的分支上进行所需的修改。完成构建和测试后，准备好与他人协作时，就可以将更改推送到托管的分支了。推送之前，你需要设置相应的上游分支；首次尝试推送到 +github+ 远程仓库时，Git 会提示你："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2029
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git push github\n"
"fatal: The current branch gnn-pr2001-fix has no upstream branch.\n"
"To push the current branch and set the remote as upstream, use\n"
msgstr "% git push github\nfatal: The current branch gnn-pr2001-fix has no upstream branch.\nTo push the current branch and set the remote as upstream, use\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2031
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "    git push --set-upstream github gnn-pr2001-fix\n"
msgstr "    git push --set-upstream github gnn-pr2001-fix\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2034
#, fuzzy
msgid "Setting the push as +git+ advises allows it to succeed:"
msgstr "按照 +git+ 的建议设置推送目标后，推送即可成功："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/committers-guide/_index.adoc:2052
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git push --set-upstream github gnn-feature\n"
"Enumerating objects: 20486, done.\n"
"Counting objects: 100% (20486/20486), done.\n"
"Delta compression using up to 8 threads\n"
"Compressing objects: 100% (12202/12202), done.\n"
"Writing objects: 100% (20180/20180), 56.25 MiB | 13.15 MiB/s, done.\n"
"Total 20180 (delta 11316), reused 12972 (delta 7770), pack-reused 0\n"
"remote: Resolving deltas: 100% (11316/11316), completed with 247 local objects.\n"
"remote:\n"
"remote: Create a pull request for 'gnn-feature' on GitHub by visiting:\n"
"remote:      https://github.com/gvnn3/freebsd-src/pull/new/gnn-feature\n"
"remote:\n"
"To github.com:gvnn3/freebsd-src.git\n"
" * [new branch]                gnn-feature -> gnn-feature\n"
